			"notes": "Nightly build of port/minecraft-26.3. **Hardware RT renders the world. Fix for the upside-down image.**\n\nnightly-2026-11-09-6: RT works. Every ray hits geometry (6206 of 6206), and the GPU time is about 3 ms. However, the RT image was mirrored vertically: trees hung from the top and the sky was at the bottom. The hand and HUD were upright.\n\nCause: in Minecraft 26.3, the Vulkan images are stored with OpenGL row order, so row 0 is at the bottom. The RT shader assumed it is at the top.\n\n- Ray direction, history reprojection and the lens-flare position now use the correct row order.\n\nNot tested in game. Please send a screenshot and latest.log."
		},
