			"notes": "Nightly build of port/minecraft-26.3. **Second fix for hardware RT.**\n\nGood news from nightly-2026-11-09-5: the RT shader now really runs (24,610 workgroups per frame, about 1 ms on the GPU) and sees all its resources correctly.\n\nThe next bug had the same cause: LWJGL 3.4 also does not set the geometry count of the acceleration structures automatically. As a result, every BLAS and TLAS was built empty, no ray hit a block (`0 primary hits`), and the shader drew sky everywhere. That is why the image looked like an upside-down sky.\n\n- Every acceleration structure build now sets its geometry count.\n\nNot tested in game. Please send latest.log and a screenshot. In the `RT pass:` line, \"primary hits\" should now be well above 0."
		},
